course: dictionary
lesson: 8242
title: Short forms: rh
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «rh» is an abbreviation, a short form of other words. You do not say it as one word. You read the letters, or the full words they stand for. Capital and small letters both appear, so read the context before you decide what it means.
explain: «Her blood is Rh-positive.» In science, Rh is part of a blood group, like A+ or O−. The plus or minus sign tells you the result. Doctors check the Rh factor before a blood transfusion. «Play the melody with your RH» means right hand on the piano, because the music is about which hand plays.
explain: «The air feels damp, and the RH is high today.» In weather, RH or rh means relative humidity: how much water vapour is in the air. Ask yourself what would make sense in the sentence. Music, blood and weather each use the same letters with a different meaning.
fact: rh is an abbreviation, a short form. Read the letters or the full words they stand for. Do not say it as one word.
fact: Rh (capital R, small h) is the chemical symbol for rhodium, a rare metal, and it also appears in blood groups such as A+ and O−.
fact: RH usually means right hand in piano music. RH or rh can mean relative humidity, how much water vapour is in the air.
fact: Doctors check the Rh factor, a protein that may be on red blood cells, before blood transfusions and during pregnancy.
fact: Greek words often use rh at the start, as in «rhythm», so spotting rh can be a clue about where a word comes from.
exercise: «The pianist read RH on the page and played with her right hand.» What does RH mean here? | Relative humidity | Rhodium | *Right hand | Rhythm
exercise: «The doctor checked her blood: it was Rh-negative.» What does Rh describe here? | *The Rh factor, a protein that may be on red blood cells | The water vapour in the air | A rare metal in a science book | The right hand of a pianist
exercise: The weather forecast says «RH is 80 per cent today.» What does RH mean? | Rhodium | Right hand | Rhythm | *Relative humidity, how much water vapour is in the air
test: The symbol Rh is used in science for which chemical? | Relative humidity | Rhythm | *Rhodium, a rare metal | Right hand
test: Find the word that starts with a Greek-style rh: | *rhythm | hill | castle | stood
exam: Ella reads «RH» on a piano score and on a weather chart. Which meaning fits the piano score? | Rhythm | *Right hand | Rhodium | Relative humidity
